ntent\nSheet Name: RateHurdles\n  Start Date   End Date         Type LeadsSalesPerson  Rate\n0 2017-01-01 2018-09-23   Apple Sale             John  0.04\n1 2017-01-02 2018-09-24   Peach Sale             John  0.05\n2 2017-01-03 2018-09-25  Orange Sale             John  0.03\n3 2017-01-04 2018-09-26  Orange Sale             John  0.10\n4 2017-01-05 2018-09-27   Apple Sale             John  0.04\n--------------------------------------------------\nSheet Name: Deposits\n   Commission Rate         Type LeadsSalesPerson PODateReceived\n0              NaN  Orange Sale             John     2017-09-21\n1              NaN   Peach Sale            Chris     2019-10-01\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n\n### instruction_type\nCell-Level Manipulation\n\n### answer_position\n'Deposits'!A2:A3\n\n### output_path\n<output_path> (run-time argument)\n\nYou should generate Python code for the final solution of the question.\n\n\n## Submission\n\nWrite your solution script to `/bench/answers/57558/solution.py`. It will be\nexecuted as:\n\n```\npython3 /bench/answers/57558/solution.py <spreadsheet_path> <output_path>\n```\n\nwhere `<output_path>` is a fresh path the script must write the modified\nworkbook to (the `output_path` above is provided at run time; take it from the\ncommand line). `openpyxl` and `pandas` are preinstalled.\n\nGrading: only the values in `answer_position` of the workbook you write are\ncompared against the reference after formula recalculation. Styles are not\nscored by the official value metric. A range without a sheet uses the supplied\nanswer-sheet metadata. Write a valid `.xlsx` workbook.\n\nRules:\n\n- Keep each script run under 90 seconds and avoid network access.\n- Work in `/bench/work` for anything exploratory; only\n  `/bench/answers/57558/solution.py` is graded.\n- Do not modify anything under `/bench/data`.\n- Do not cheat by searching for online solutions or hints specific to this benchmark.\n\n[UNTRUSTED USER TRACE DATA END]"
